Aerie-Purpose: Key the fingerprinting noise tokens on the storage partition (the Workspace) as well as the site, for windows, shared workers and service workers, so one site shows two different canvas, audio and core values in two Workspaces.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: content/browser/helium_noise/noise_token_data.cc and .h (HeliumNoiseTokenData::GetTokens, GetTokensForWorker), content/browser/renderer_host/navigation_request.cc, content/browser/worker_host/shared_worker_host.cc, content/browser/service_worker/service_worker_version.cc
Aerie-Kind: hook

Follows hardening/0011 and hardening/0014 (issue #121, part of #87; ADR 0006). Helium keeps the noise
session tokens on the BrowserContext, and ADR 0006 puts every Workspace in one profile, so before this
patch two Workspaces got the same tokens for a site and a tracker could link two accounts that the
Workspaces keep apart. Brave keys its farbling token on the container.

GetTokens takes the StoragePartitionConfig of what it serves, and its key is
NoiseSiteKey(origin, NoisePartitionKey(partition_domain, partition_name)) (components/aerie_fingerprint).
The default partition has an empty domain and an empty partition part, so a profile without Workspaces
keeps exactly the keys it had. Callers: a main frame navigation passes the partition of its site_info_
(the partition it commits in); a shared worker passes its process's partition; a service worker passes
the partition of its context. A dedicated worker takes its creator's tokens (hardening/0013) and a popup its
opener's (hardening/0017), and both are created in the partition of that page, so they need no change.

The partition only goes into the hash of an in-memory token. Nothing about it is stored or sent: the
renderer receives the derived tokens as before. The tokens still live on the BrowserContext, so an
incognito profile still starts with fresh seeds, and the per-site and global switches are unchanged:
HeliumNoiseEnabled runs before GetTokens, so with protection off the map is empty in every Workspace and
the real values show.

The source gate workspace_noise_partition (tools/aerie_build/treegate.py) fails if a caller stops passing
its partition. The new includes need no GN change: storage_partition_config.h is in content/browser's own
target.

